Getting married in a château in the Loire Valley is a dream come true, but one question always springs to mind first: how much does it actually cost? The answer depends on the region, the season and what you mean by ‘château’. Here are the actual figures, item by item, and our rates at La Huberdière, in Touraine near Amboise, 2 hours and 20 minutes from Paris.

This guide distinguishes between the venue hire fee and the overall budget for the day. The two are often lumped together in searches, even though they are completely different.

## How much does it cost to hire a castle for a wedding?

The cost of hiring a château for a wedding in France usually ranges from €4,000 to €15,000, with the variation largely depending on the region. Around Paris, the most sought-after venues cost over €10,000, and sometimes as much as €15,000 for a weekend. In the provinces, and particularly in the Loire Valley, you can find charming venues starting from €4,000 to €6,000.

This price covers exclusive use of the venue: the château, its reception rooms and the grounds, often including an overnight stay on site. It varies according to three simple factors. Firstly, the season: a Saturday in June or September costs more than a Friday in October. Secondly, the duration: a single day or a full weekend. Finally, the level of service: from a bare venue that you furnish yourself to a fully equipped estate.

## The overall wedding budget, item by item

The total budget for a wedding with 100 guests in France is between €12,000 and €20,000, and the venue hire accounts for only a portion of that. Here is the breakdown we most commonly see among the couples we work with.

- Catering: between €80 and €180 per guest, making it the biggest expense for an event with around a hundred guests
- Château hire: from €4,000 to €8,000 in the Loire Valley for exclusive use
- Drinks: from €15 to €40 per person, or less if you bring your own wine
- Decor and flowers: from €1,500 to €4,000, depending on the theme
- Music, DJ or band: from €800 to €2,500
- The photographer and videographer: from €1,500 to €4,000
- Dresses, suits and outfits: from €1,500 to €5,000

Furniture deserves a mention of its own. Some venues charge extra for it. At La Huberdière, we offer it for €15 per person, including tables and chairs, to avoid having to hire from outside, which can quickly drive up the bill.

## The Loire Valley or Île-de-France: the price difference

For the same level of service, a wedding château in the Loire Valley often costs 30 to 50 per cent less than its equivalent in Île-de-France. Demand around Paris is so high that the most sought-after venues charge between €10,000 and €15,000 for exclusive use, whilst a charming château in Touraine costs between €4,000 and €8,000.

This price difference does not come at the expense of quality – quite the opposite, in fact. The Loire Valley is home to France’s finest heritage: inhabited stately homes, landscaped parks and a time-honoured tradition of hospitality. The Parisian premium stems from the proximity and the scarcity of available slots, not from the charm of the venues themselves. For guests travelling from the capital, a 2-hour 20-minute drive or an hour’s journey by TGV to Saint-Pierre-des-Corps turns the journey into the start of the weekend, without weighing heavily against the thousands of euros saved on the rental.

## What is the most expensive part of a castle wedding?

The catering is almost always the biggest expense, far ahead of the venue hire. With 100 guests at €120 per person, the meal alone comes to over €12,000. This is where the bulk of your budget is spent – far more so than on the choice of château.

Next comes the venue, followed by a range of secondary elements: flowers, music, visuals and outfits. The good news is that a castle’s reception hall often serves as a substitute for a marquee, along with its décor and furnishings. A beautiful park and stately stone buildings provide part of the backdrop, which in turn simplifies the décor.

## Our private hire rates at La Huberdière

At La Huberdière, hiring the estate exclusively for a wedding costs between €4,000 and €8,000 depending on the season, and you have the venue all to yourselves. No other groups, no other events taking place at the same time: the château, its four reception rooms, the 14-hectare grounds and the swimming pool are all yours and your guests’ to enjoy.

The private hire package includes the indoor and outdoor reception areas, as well as use of the grounds for both the secular ceremony and the drinks reception. We are open all year round, which means we can host autumn and winter weddings – which are more affordable and just as beautiful under the tall trees.

Two options often make all the difference to the final budget. Furniture at €15 per person, which saves you from having to hire it from outside. And the corkage fee, which allows you to bring your own wines and champagnes rather than paying the caterer’s prices. For full details of our packages and to arrange a viewing, please visit our dedicated page for [organising your wedding at the château](/en/mariage).

## Accommodating guests on site

Accommodating some of your guests at the château avoids the need for shuttle buses and keeps the party going longer – and this is an expense that many couples overlook when drawing up their budget. La Huberdière has 10 bedrooms, sleeping a total of 21 people, spread throughout the house. Your closest family and friends can stay on site, whilst the rest of the guests can find accommodation in Amboise and Nazelles-Négron, just a few minutes away.

This accommodation is available as part of a private weekend hire. To give your guests something to do the following day, our guide to [visiting the châteaux of the Loire Valley](/en/blog/visiter-chateaux-de-la-loire) introduces them to the region, and our [charming guest rooms](/en/sejour) allow them to extend their stay in peaceful surroundings. If you’re mainly bringing together close friends and family, our article on [renting a château with friends and family](/en/blog/louer-chateau-entre-amis-famille) provides further inspiration.

## How to keep your castle wedding budget under control

You can have a lovely wedding at the château without breaking the bank by focusing on three key factors: the date, the number of guests and independent suppliers. A Friday or Sunday costs less than a Saturday in peak season. An autumn wedding in the Loire Valley offers the same setting for a more affordable exclusive hire fee.

The number of guests remains the real deciding factor: each guest has an impact on the catering, drinks and stationery. An intimate wedding of 40 to 60 people falls well below the national averages, and the château lends itself particularly well to this. Finally, a venue that allows you to choose your own caterer and bring your own wine, as we do, puts you in control of the two most costly aspects. To explore the planning process in more detail beyond the budget, our guide to [organising a wedding at a château](/en/blog/organiser-mariage-au-chateau) covers all the other questions you’ll need to ask yourself.

Let us know your date, the number of guests and the theme of your wedding: we’ll send you a detailed quote within 24 hours.
